## Why I Mentor (the real answer, not the interview answer)

I learned on my own, with no guide. I wasted precious time tinkering and finding my way around - things that could've taken 3 months took closer to a year because there was no one to point the way.

I don't want someone else to go through that same waste.

Over the years I've trained students directly - including students who didn't believe they could be in tech at first. Many of my own mentees are now working in great companies across Nigeria and a few outside the country.

I enjoy passing on knowledge, helping people cross bridges that seemed difficult, and helping them avoid the avoidable mistakes.

**The core of it:** I simply want to see my mentees rise, and know I played a part in their journey.

